{"slug":"suesser-brei","title":"Der süße Brei","theme":"Märchen","source":"Der süße Brei (1857)","pairs":[{"de":"Es war einmal ein armes frommes Mädchen, das lebte mit seiner Mutter allein, und sie hatten nichts mehr zu essen. Da gieng das Kind hinaus in den Wald, und begegnete ihm da eine alte Frau, die wußte seinen Jammer schon und schenkte ihm ein Töpfchen, zu dem sollt es sagen „Töpfchen, koche,“ so kochte es guten süßen Hirsenbrei, und wenn es sagte „Töpfchen, steh,“ so hörte es wieder auf zu kochen. Das Mädchen brachte den Topf seiner Mutter heim, und nun waren sie ihrer Armuth und ihres Hungers ledig und aßen süßen Brei so oft sie wollten.","en":"There was once a poor, pious girl who lived alone with her mother, and they had nothing left to eat. So the child went out into the forest, and there an old woman met her who already knew her trouble, and gave her a little pot. She was to say to it, “Little pot, cook,” and it would cook good sweet millet porridge; and when she said, “Little pot, stop,” it would leave off cooking again. The girl brought the pot home to her mother, and now they were rid of their poverty and their hunger, and ate sweet porridge as often as they liked."},{"de":"Auf eine Zeit war das Mädchen ausgegangen, da sprach die Mutter „Töpfchen, koche,“ da kocht es, und sie ißt sich satt; nun will sie daß das Töpfchen wieder aufhören soll, aber sie weiß das Wort nicht. Also kocht es fort, und der Brei steigt über den Rand hinaus und kocht immer zu, die Küche und das ganze Haus voll, und das zweite Haus und dann die Straße, als wollts die ganze Welt satt machen, und ist die größte Noth, und kein Mensch weiß sich da zu helfen.","en":"One day the girl had gone out, and her mother said, “Little pot, cook.” And it cooked, and she ate her fill; and now she wanted the little pot to stop again, but she did not know the word. So it went on cooking, and the porridge rose over the rim and kept on cooking — the kitchen full, and the whole house, and the second house, and then the street, as though it meant to feed the whole world; and it was the greatest distress, and not a soul knew how to help."},{"de":"Endlich, wie nur noch ein einziges Haus übrig ist, da kommt das Kind heim, und spricht nur „Töpfchen, steh,“ da steht es und hört auf zu kochen; und wer wieder in die Stadt wollte, der mußte sich durchessen.","en":"At last, when only one single house was left, the child came home and said nothing but “Little pot, stop,” and it stood still and left off cooking; and whoever wanted to go back into the town had to eat their way through."}],"lemmaMap":{"Es":[{"lemma":"Es","confidence":1,"method":"exact"},{"lemma":"E","confidence":0.95,"method":"wiktionary"}],"war":[{"lemma":"sein","confidence":0.95,"method":"wiktionary"},{"lemma":"einsein","confidence":0.48,"method":"separable"},{"lemma":"war","confidence":0.25,"method":"exact"}],"einmal":[{"lemma":"einmal","confidence":1,"method":"exact"}],"ein":[{"lemma":"ein","confidence":1,"method":"exact"}],"Mädchen":[{"lemma":"Mädchen","confidence":1,"method":"exact"},{"lemma":"Mädch","confidence":0.5,"method":"suffix"},{"lemma":"Madch","confidence":0.45,"method":"suffix"},{"lemma":"Mädche","confidence":0.4,"method":"suffix"},{"lemma":"Madchen","confidence":0.4,"method":"suffix"},{"lemma":"Madche","confidence":0.35000000000000003,"method":"suffix"}],"das":[{"lemma":"das","confidence":1,"method":"exact"},{"lemma":"der","confidence":0.95,"method":"wiktionary"},{"lemma":"mitder","confidence":0.48,"method":"separable"}],"armes":[{"lemma":"arm","confidence":0.95,"method":"wiktionary"},{"lemma":"arme","confidence":0.4,"method":"suffix"},{"lemma":"armes","confidence":0.25,"method":"exact"}],"frommes":[{"lemma":"fromm","confidence":0.95,"method":"wiktionary"},{"lemma":"fromme","confidence":0.4,"method":"suffix"},{"lemma":"frommes","confidence":0.25,"method":"exact"}],"Mutter":[{"lemma":"Mutter","confidence":1,"method":"exact"},{"lemma":"Mutt","confidence":0.45,"method":"suffix"}],"lebte":[{"le